// The keyboard for `click_counter.ron`.
//
// One binding, and it sends the same action the button's `hitrect` sends. That
// is the point of the pair: a click and a key reach the simulation as the same
// `buy 1`, and nothing downstream can tell which one happened. A recording of
// either replays into the same counter (ADR-0012's M5.2 amendment - the
// recording is at the action level, so the device is outside the closure).
//
// `OnPress` and not `OnPressAndRelease`: buying is something that happens once,
// and a release value would be an event every consumer had to know to ignore
// (ADR-0025).
Mapping(
    bindings: [
        (control: Space, action: "buy", emit: OnPress(1)),
    ],
)
